  "termination": "completed",
  "answer": "All three modules are updated and consistent. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Summary\n\nI extended the formatting options across all three modules while preserving the existing exports and behavior.\n\n### `defaults.mjs`\n- Added `unitLabel: ''` to `DEFAULT_OPTIONS`, giving `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: '' }`.\n- Wrapped it in `Object.freeze(...)` so the defaults can never be mutated.\n\n### `resolver.mjs`\n- Rewrote `resolveOptions(overrides)` to **return a fresh object** built from the defaults instead of mutating and returning the shared `DEFAULT_OPTIONS` (the old code had a mutation bug).\n- `undefined` (or no argument) means no overrides.\n- Rejects `null`, non-objects, and arrays with `TypeError`.\n- Rejects unknown keys with `TypeError` (only `precision`, `prefix`, `unitLabel` allowed).\n- Validates `precision` as an integer 0–4, throwing `RangeError` otherwise.\n- Validates `prefix` and `unitLabel` as strings, throwing `TypeError` otherwise.\n- Only own fields override defaults (uses `hasOwnProperty`).\n\n### `formatter.mjs`\n- `formatValue(value, overrides)` now rejects non-finite/non-number values with `TypeError`.\n- Delegates option resolution to `resolveOptions`.\n- Appends `\" \" + unitLabel` after the formatted number when `unitLabel` is nonempty.\n- Preserves old call forms.\n\n### Verified behavior\n- `formatValue(12.345)` → `\"12.35\"`\n- `formatValue(12.34, { precision: 1, prefix: '~' })` → `\"~12.3\"`\n- `formatValue(12.3, { unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"12.30 kg\"`\n- `formatValue(12.3, { precision: 1, prefix: '~', unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `\"~12.3 kg\"`\n- `resolveOptions({ unitLabel: 'kg' })` → `{ precision: 2, prefix: '', unitLabel: 'kg' }`\n\nNo shared mutable state exists: defaults are frozen, and every `resolveOptions` call returns a new object. I did not modify `public.test.mjs` (it was not in scope for editing).",
